<!-- FAQ SECTION -->
<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">FAQs - IT Notice Section 147 in Pune</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Find answers to the most common questions about Section 147 reassessment in Pune.</p>
                    @include('partials.bigin-form', [
                        'variant'  => 'compact',
                        'service'  => 'IT Notice Section 147 in Pune',
                        'city'     => 'Pune',
                    ])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Section 147 reassessment?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Section 147 authorizes AO to assess or reassess income for a prior AY if credible information shows income escaped assessment. Different from scrutiny (current year). Reopens completed assessments. Begins with Section 148A show cause notice, then formal Section 148 notice if AO decides to proceed. Can apply whether or not return was originally filed.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the difference between Section 147 and Section 148?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Section 147 is the charging section giving AO the power to reassess. Section 148 is the procedural section prescribing the notice mechanism. Section 148A is the safeguard - mandatory pre-notice inquiry with taxpayer hearing. You receive 148A(b) SCN first, then 148 notice with 148A(d) order, then actual reassessment happens under Section 147.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the time limit for reassessment?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Post Finance Act 2024 (01-09-2024): 3 years 3 months from end of relevant AY if escaped income below Rs 50 lakh; 5 years 3 months if Rs 50 lakh or more. Example: AY 2022-23 normal limit June 2026 (3yr 3mo); extended June 2028 if escaped income >= Rs 50 lakh. AO cannot reopen beyond these limits. Patron verifies time limit for every notice.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I challenge the reassessment notice?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Under GKN Driveshafts (SC 2003), you can file written objections on grounds: time limit violation (S.149), 148A non-compliance, S.151 approval defect (Rajeev Bansal SC 2024 - mechanical approval = void), no credible information, or change of opinion. AO must dispose objections by speaking order. If notice invalid, entire reassessment is void.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is Section 148A and why is it important?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Mandatory pre-notice procedure since 01-04-2021. AO must: inquiry with specified authority approval, SCN sharing all evidence, 7-30 day response window, reasoned order under 148A(d). A Section 148 notice issued without following 148A is void. This is the taxpayer's first and best opportunity to prevent reassessment - a well-drafted response can stop it before it begins.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if I don't respond?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Non-response to 148A SCN means AO proceeds without your input - 148 notice almost certain. Non-compliance with 148 notice leads to Best Judgment Assessment under Section 144 with maximum additions and higher demand. Penalties under S.270A may also be imposed. You lose opportunity to present your case at assessment stage, though appeal rights remain.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is reassessment different from scrutiny?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Fundamentally different. Scrutiny (S.143(2)) examines current year return before completing assessment - forward-looking. Reassessment (S.147) reopens a completed prior year assessment when new information shows escaped income - backward-looking. Reassessment has stricter procedural requirements (148A, time limits, approval) because it disturbs finality.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the Rs 50 lakh threshold?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Determines time limit for reassessment post 01-09-2024. Below Rs 50 lakh escaped: 3yr 3mo. Rs 50 lakh or more: 5yr 3mo. Also determines approval level under S.151. Minimum threshold: Rs 1 lakh escaped income required (unless search/survey).</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Section 147 ka notice aaya toh kya karein?</strong> Pehle 148A SCN ka jawab 7-30 din mein dein - yeh sabse important step hai. Agar 148 notice aaye toh return file karein aur GKN Driveshafts objection dein. CA ki madad bahut zaroori hai. Patron Pune office se sab handle karta hai.</p><p><strong>Time limit kya hai?</strong> 3 saal 3 mahine (< Rs 50L) / 5 saal 3 mahine (>= Rs 50L) from end of relevant AY (01-09-2024 ke baad).</p><p><strong>Penalty kya hogi?</strong> Agar respond nahi kiya toh Best Judgment Assessment S.144. Penalty S.270A (50-200%). Prosecution severe cases mein.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

